{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/290419-seeds-of-life-3-and-trans-issues","id":290419,"title":"Seeds of life 3 and Trans issues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-23T05:00:04-07:00","id":290419,"title":"Seeds of life 3 and Trans issues","content":"SORRY WRONG FORUM, COULD ANY MODERATOR SHIFT THIS TO MUMMY FORUM?<br /> <br /> <br /> What happens when an &quot;heterosexual&quot; coupe with an operated transgender is under the effect of the last unleash of the Seeds of Life Utterance?<br /> <br /> If a MTF couples with a man, is it considered an heterosexual intercourse for Seeds of Life? What effects would it take?<br /> If a MTF couples with a woman, is it considered homosexual and thus doesn't work?<br /> And vice versa<br /> <br /> I asked this because what we choose to define someone for ethical reasons, is not necessarily what something ancient and monolithic like Sekhem magic would define. I mean, ethically, we call a MTF a woman because that's what she chose to be, but I don't personally think Sekhem magic would consider it a woman.<br /> To consider her a woman by magic, I think it would take a <b>supernal</b> Life and Prime magic spell, or a shift into her <b>supernal</b> symbols.<br /> <br /> What's your interpretation on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T11:16:00-07:00","id":290675,"title":"","content":"I think sekhem is even more unlikely to putz around with silly things like chromosomes or whatever more &quot;objective&quot; terms you might use to define sex. <br /> <br /> All magic is symbolic on some level or another (just like all words are symbolic, and all thoughts are symbolic), that's not something supernal magic has a corner on. The spell already overwrites material reality (infertility induced by age, injury, chromosomal irregularity, or intentional intercession) with a symbolic 'truth' (&quot;this is a woman and a woman is fertile&quot;), why would it have trouble with an easier symbolic truth like &quot;this is a woman&quot; (All sex and all gender being symbolic anyway)?<br /> <br /> In other words, I'd let it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T11:30:14-07:00","id":290682,"title":"","content":"Seeds of life isn't inherently impressive, until you open it up to the infinite possible combinations of things that &quot;could&quot; get pregnant.<br /> Changelings, werewolves and wolves, Mummies of either gender, human and bull, Prometheans, Ghosts, Ghost and human, two men or two women, Demons, Angels, Whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T12:37:06-07:00","id":290721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/290419-seeds-of-life-3-and-trans-issues?p=290682#post290682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummies of either gender, [...]two men or two women, Demons, Angels, Whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>A cursed target\u2019s next mating with an adult partner of theopposite sex results in automatic conception. [from MtC corebook]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T12:54:28-07:00","id":290730,"title":"","content":"That's a tricky question. One one hand, magic in mummy isn't &quot;Supernal&quot;--it's largely a palpable, material force. The Utterance also specifies sex, not gender. We could substitute gender for sex as suggested, but this isn't necessarily a politically restorative act, because not all trans identities reject birth bodies' common biological roles in childbirth--transmen have carried pregnancies to term and transwomen have impregnated others without compromising who they are one bit.<br /> <br /> However, later Egyptian culture did accept adopting gendered symbols as a magical-political act, along with the notion that there *is* a symbolic form of gender beyond personal gender identity. For example, Hatshepsut wore a false beard, but male counterparts *also* wore one. So neither self-identification as a man nor male biological attributes were the same as divine-Pharaonic gender.<br /> <br /> So really, you can take it a number of ways, relying of course on players with trans identities to help define the parameters for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 10-23-2014, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T13:10:06-07:00","id":290738,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean, sex isn't really a real thing either, it's a symbolic imposition of a duality on something that's a lot wibblier (wibbly is a totally specific term, just go with it). The spell already accepts that symbolic duality and operates with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T14:07:21-07:00","id":290780,"title":"","content":"This is true--what the spell does to strongly intersexed individuals is an interesting question. It's worth noting that the consensus of how Akhenaten is portrayed as art has shifted away from a new realism movement to the theory that some of his characteristics were meant to suggest stereotypically female traits that imply fertility and creative power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:50:18-07:00","id":290827,"title":"","content":"I don't really think that the Utterance is intended to create a biologically-functional uterus or ovaries/testes where there are none existing (or never was one, in the case of the Utterance reversing vasectomy, hysterectomy, or tubal ligation). So if a cis woman has underwent menopause, the Utterance will reverse that process (which is just a byproduct of aging and loss of a finite resource), basically I guess using magic to empower the woman's ovaries to make more eggs (leaving aside the fact that the ovaries don't make more eggs after a certain stage in fetal development...). For a cis man who is &quot;shooting blanks,&quot; the Utterance would basically fix whatever is wrong with his testes and allow them to manufacture viable sperm. And I think it's important to note that none of the magic of Irem really cared about what the individual wanted (unless the individual was a member of the Shan'iatu), but instead followed cosmic metaphysical rules. I think it might be a little out of theme for Mummy magic to prioritize an individual's mental needs/wants for their body over simply reinforcing the existing fleshly pattern which is much more of a &quot;known quantity&quot; for the magic to interact with.<br /> <br /> You do raise an interesting question, but here it might be instructive to reference Hebeny: at low Memory, Hebeny appears much more masculine, while as his Memory rises, the sadhu takes on the characteristics of &quot;remembering&quot; the physical body as it was thousands of years ago, which was quite busty and feminine. I can't imagine the frustration and dysphoria that must result when Hebeny is at high Memory, knowing that there is no way to permanently change his body short of becoming Twice-Arisen (which he seems to find heretical to do for such a &quot;trivial&quot; reason, if at all). Basically, Hebeny's body manifestation is directly affected by the ancient magic of the Rite of Return, presenting the physical factual reality of the distant past over longstanding desires of the mind (and soul - though the soul would seem to be betraying Hebeny at high Memory, forcing an unwanted form, but I digress).<br /> <br /> For a very intersexed individual, I think it would depend on what biologically-functional organs were present. I think this could get quite complicated (I am not near enough familiar on the real-world medicine to hard a guess on what is possible or has been medically documented) and possibly even result in a person who could both sire and bear children. I think this is territory where it's best left up to the player and ST to decide what works best for the story in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T18:41:45-07:00","id":290932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/290419-seeds-of-life-3-and-trans-issues?p=290721#post290721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cursed target\u2019s next mating with an adult partner of theopposite sex results in automatic conception. [from MtC corebook]</div> </div> </div> </div>Open your mind, it's a third tier utterance that does nothing but guaranty a baby.<br /> <br /> But of course if its easier feel free obey what the writer has written word for word. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T23:07:56-07:00","id":291077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/290419-seeds-of-life-3-and-trans-issues?p=290932#post290932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Open your mind, it's a third tier utterance that does nothing but guaranty a baby.<br /> <br /> But of course if its easier feel free obey what the writer has written word for word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, first, it's a curse. Second, the MTF was born male, and its chromosomes created a male. Whatever gender we assing to her it's just political correctness (sorry to any trans person reading the thread, I mean no offense, it's just that I think Sekhem doesn't consider social norms at all). My interpretation is that an operated MTF having sex with a woman would regain testes and penis (much to her disappointment). A MTF and a male partner wouldn't be affected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You do raise an interesting question, but here it might be instructive to reference Hebeny: at low Memory, Hebeny appears much more masculine, while as his Memory rises, the sadhu takes on the characteristics of &quot;remembering&quot; the physical body as it was thousands of years ago, which was quite busty and feminine. I can't imagine the frustration and dysphoria that must result when Hebeny is at high Memory, knowing that there is no way to permanently change his body short of becoming Twice-Arisen (which he seems to find heretical to do for such a &quot;trivial&quot; reason, if at all). Basically, Hebeny's body manifestation is directly affected by the ancient magic of the Rite of Return, presenting the physical factual reality of the distant past over longstanding desires of the mind (and soul - though the soul would seem to be betraying Hebeny at high Memory, forcing an unwanted form, but I digress). </div> </div> </div>In which book is Hebeny mentioned? Plus, I'm quite convinced the sahu is based on a subjective perception, while what the Utterance affects is a material, purely biological purview, not one of the mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I said before about supernal magic, is that it would take supernal magic to allow sekhem magic to consider her a woman for magic. But I think also that &quot;changeling&quot; magic, which works more on the context and can paraphrase it, would certainly work despite her being born a male. Doubtful of Gifts and Transmutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T23:41:31-07:00","id":291084,"title":"","content":"Hebeny is a character in Cursed Necropolis D.C.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the strangest thing about all this is that someone would actually bother to get Seeds of Life and be sure to get to Tier 3. The preceding tiers aren't all that great (unless you're playing in an earlier time period, in which case the first tier is awesome), and the third one is rather unlikely to have an impact without a very particular kind of game structure. I think Waters of Life and Death is the only other Utterance out there that's as unimpressive as Seeds of Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T02:52:47-07:00","id":291158,"title":"","content":"Seeds of life is quite underpowered on the whole. Allowing pregnancy and regenerating sexual organs isn't as powerful as other Tier 3 powers. It's at most a Tier 1 power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T03:53:25-07:00","id":291166,"title":"","content":"Yep, pretty much my thoughts on the subject. The first Tier is pretty neat. Snake-making, resistance to arrows and spears and other wooden weapons, and the ability to cure point all for one Pillar point. If you're running a historical setting that predates gunpowder, I'd almost go so far as to say that the first tier is good enough on its own to account for all the others. In the modern day, it gets scaled back to &quot;situationally great&quot;.<br /> <br /> The bonus the second tier gives in social situations to those who eat the fruit is neat, but if you compare it to other social abilities (Dreams of Dead Gods and Word of the Amanuensis, namely), it's pretty lacklustre by comparison. Those utterances don't have to deal with the issue of getting someone to eat food you grew before they can have an effect, either.<br /> <br /> And, as you say, the third tier is actually kind of laughable. Short of playing a chronicle that jumps decades at a time, you're never going to see the impact of it on the world. And even if you do, well, the only benefit it could logically provide would be a way of producing a large cult made entirely of Witnesses.<br /> <br /> It's not as bad as Waters of Life and Death, but it is one of the very small handful of Mummy powers that are decidedly unimpressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T07:59:31-07:00","id":291340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/290419-seeds-of-life-3-and-trans-issues?p=290932#post290932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Open your mind, it's a third tier utterance that does nothing but guaranty a baby.<br /> <br /> But of course if its easier feel free obey what the writer has written word for word.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you first read the book and AFTER write about... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> dont open a flame, please.<br /> We're discussing RAW, not Rules As I Want Them To Be.<br /> <br /> If you put as your idea for &quot;upgrade&quot; a power, you are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-24-2014, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:09:46-07:00","id":291483,"title":"","content":"Seeds of Life, particularly Tier 3, empowers a particular character type. There are ample plots a character could unleash by being an unholy font of fertility, and ample favors having such a power could bring him.<br /> <br /> That said it is pretty weak on a mechanical level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T17:44:05-07:00","id":292553,"title":"","content":"Given that the utterance can regenerate amputated organs, I see no reason that it would be unable to modify or create what is needed. I think for the curse to work someone in the couple has to identify as male and the other as female. Assuming you have that, the magic should alter bodies as needed to make it work out.<br /> <br /> There are intersex people with a mixture of male and female characteristics. Some have both XX and XY DNA, in different parts of their bodies. When it comes to strict procreation requirements it would seem there isn't that much difference. Males and females have analogous parts.<br /> <br /> Basically, there is nothing the utterance can do to enable a person to sire or gestate a child that is stranger than what can already occur in nature. There are actually less advanced animals that can change their sex in a single generation. I would force body changes as necessary to make it work out. For homosexuals, it just wouldn't do anything. Somebody has to identify as male and the other female. I think anything beyond that is a real stretch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T18:09:11-07:00","id":292563,"title":"","content":"I just don't think Iremite magic cares at all about individual beliefs on gender identity; it's more a matter of hacking a universal source code than anything else. I could see a conservative Mummy believing some version of &quot;the gods saw fit to make your body with a penis, not breasts and a vagina; it is a devil in your head or raw foolishness that makes you believe you are a woman.&quot; I could see their magic working on the same paradigm. For intersex, as frequently happens IRL I expect sex would be assigned at birth (possibly with crude surgery; possibly the child would be left to die of exposure for not being &quot;normal&quot;) but if assigned a binary sex, would be expected to live up to the societal roles of that sex for the rest of their life, and that would be the &quot;assumed&quot; sex for purposes of the Utterance.<br /> <br /> Yes this is hugely transphobic; however, what we would call progressive liberalism and respect for individual self-determination of any person in ancient cultures is quite rare, but for those straddling the top of their society (and even then, being Pharaoh or Emperor didn't mean you could marry a man and expect social acceptability, even if you might have had men in your harem for sex). Hell, this is not an uncommon attitude among certain political affiliations today.<br /> <br /> For all that there are pop culture jokes about Greco-Roman tolerance of homosexuality, there was still immense stigma in a man serving in the &quot;feminine&quot; or receptive role of either oral or anal sex and an expectation that men would marry women and create new family units. IRL, trans issues are still hugely marginalized compared to gay/lesbian rights; I see no reason to believe that super-ancient necromancy is going to be more progressive.<br /> <br /> I mean certainly, if a man has undescended testicles and that causes sterility, or a man has his prostate removed due to cancer, the Utterance should reverse those states, but I don't believe it's going to suddenly generate a biologically-functional prostate and testicles on the body of a transman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-26-2014, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T00:30:48-07:00","id":292776,"title":"","content":"I would say it would work... but only on post-op transexuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to 